# Raphael, Most Attitude: "you may play a card exiled with Raphael" is "play", so a land card exiled with him is a land play
# (CR 305.1), and the timing rules still apply (his rulings). Turn 1: Raphael, then an Ornithopter whose trigger exiles the top
# card, a Forest. Turn 3: after he attacks, the Forest still can't be played during combat; in the second main phase it can,
# as the turn's land play - the Mountain in hand is then refused, since the land play is used.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Ruby
Raphael, Most Attitude
Ornithopter
Mountain
Mountain
Mountain
Forest
Mountain x12

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Raphael, Most Attitude.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Accept
? Exile.Count = 1
[T3 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Raphael, Most Attitude > Bot2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Exile.Forest.Play
[T3 Bot1.Main2]
Bot1.Exile.Forest.Play
! Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Tapped = false
Exile.Count = 0
Bot2.Life = 16
